            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7210-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7210 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`xml.parsers.expat` and `xml.etree.ElementTree` use insufficient entropy for Expat hash-flooding protection, which allows a crafted XML document to trigger hash flooding.\\r\\n\\r\\nFully mitigating this vulnerability requires both updating libexpat to 2.8.0 or later and applying this patch."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7210",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-7210\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-7210](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7210)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-7210**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpython3.12-minimal  | 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.15  |   | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-7210](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7210)  |\n"
