            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-51304-libsqlite3-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-51304 medium vulnerability for libsqlite3-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "sqlite 3.41 has a use-after-free (UAF) vulnerability in the ORDER BY clause parsing routine. The affected code first releases the memory of an ExprList object via sqlite3ExprListDelete(), then attempts to access the nExpr member of the already freed object. This dangling pointer access causes invalid memory read operations. By constructing a malicious SQL statement containing an ORDER BY clause with a large number of items, a remote adversary can trigger this vulnerability. Successful exploitation can result in application crash (denial of service), leakage of sensitive memory contents, and under certain memory layout conditions, arbitrary code execution on the affected system."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-51304",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-51304\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nVersion: 3.45.1-1ubuntu2.7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-51304](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-51304)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-51304**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libsqlite3-0  | 3.45.1-1ubuntu2.7  |   | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-51304](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-51304)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libsqlite3-0@3.45.1-1ubuntu2.7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=sqlite3"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41992-gzip",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41992 medium vulnerability for gzip package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU gzip contains a global buffer overflow vulnerability in the LZH decompression logic caused by improper reuse of shared global state between different decompression formats within a single execution. GNU gzip maintains a global array that is shared across the LZ77, LZW, and LZH decompression routines and is not reinitialized between files processed in the same invocation.\nBy decompressing a specially crafted LZW file followed by a specially crafted LZH file in a single gzip -d command, an attacker can poison the shared global state and subsequently trigger an out‑of‑bounds read in the LZH decoder. The LZH decompression logic follows stale values left in the shared array, causing reads past the end of the allocated global buffer.\n\nThis issue has been fixed in the commit 63dbf6b3b9e6e781df1a6a64e609b10e23969681"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: gzip\nVersion: 1.12-1ubuntu3.1\nFix Version: 1.12-1ubuntu3.2\nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-41992](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | gzip  | 1.12-1ubuntu3.1  | 1.12-1ubuntu3.2  | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-41992](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/gzip@1.12-1ubuntu3.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54411-libpam-modules",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54411 medium vulnerability for libpam-modules package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Linux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences. The comparison uses strncmp() (or strncasecmp() when PAM_ICASE_ARG is set) preceded by a length-equality check, so the time to reject a candidate depends on the index of the first differing byte and on whether the candidate's length matches the stored password, leaking the password length and individual prefix bytes. The vulnerable path is reached when the administrator configures pam_userdb with crypt=none, with an unrecognized crypt method, or without a crypt= argument, causing the module to store and compare credentials in plaintext."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54411",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54411\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpam-modules\nVersion: 1.5.3-5ubuntu5.5\nFix Version: 1.5.3-5ubuntu5.6\nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-54411](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54411)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54411**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpam-modules  | 1.5.3-5ubuntu5.5  | 1.5.3-5ubuntu5.6  | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-54411](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54411)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libpam-modules@1.5.3-5ubuntu5.5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=pam"
