            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48962-libperl5.38t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48962 medium vulnerability for libperl5.38t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Compress versions before 2.220 for Perl can execute arbitrary code in File::GlobMapper via an attacker-controlled output glob.\n\n_parseOutputGlob() wraps the caller-supplied output glob string in double quotes and stores it in the parser state; _getFiles() then runs the stored expression through eval STRING. A literal double quote in the output glob closes the dquote wrapper, and the characters that follow are evaluated as Perl.\n\nArbitrary Perl in the output glob executes at the calling process's privilege."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48962\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libperl5.38t64\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-48962](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48962**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libperl5.38t64  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-48962](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libperl5.38t64@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
