            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-51300-libsqlite3-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-51300 medium vulnerability for libsqlite3-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in the expression parsing and memory management logic of SQLite 3.41. After invoking sqlite3ExprDelete to release an expression object, the program still retains the dangling pointer and subsequently accesses member fields of the already freed memory. By constructing malicious SQL queries, a remote attacker can trigger invalid memory access, leading to application crash and sensitive memory information leakage."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-51300",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-51300\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nVersion: 3.45.1-1ubuntu2.7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-51300](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-51300)",
