                "text": "A vulnerability has been found in GNU ncurses up to 6.5-20250322 and classified as problematic. This vulnerability affects the function postprocess_termcap of the file tinfo/parse_entry.c. The manipulation leads to stack-based buffer overflow. The attack needs to be approached locally. Upgrading to version 6.5-20250329 is able to address this issue. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-6141",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-6141\nSeverity: low\nPackage: ncurses-bin\nVersion: 6.4+20240113-1ubuntu2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2025-6141](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-6141)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-6141**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | ncurses-bin  | 6.4+20240113-1ubuntu2  |   | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2025-6141](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-6141)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/ncurses-bin@6.4%2B20240113-1ubuntu2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=ncurses"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54370-libacl1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54370 medium vulnerability for libacl1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "acl before version 2.4.0 contains a time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability that allows local attackers to escalate privileges by replacing a pathname component with a symbolic link between an lstat() check and subsequent symlink-following operations such as stat(), chown(), chmod(), acl_get_file(), and acl_set_file(). Attackers who control a pathname component can redirect file access control list operations to arbitrary files when getfacl, setfacl, or chacl is invoked by a privileged process over an attacker-controlled path, resulting in local privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libacl1\nVersion: 2.3.2-1build1.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: \nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libacl1  | 2.3.2-1build1.1  |   | deb  |   | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libacl1@2.3.2-1build1.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=acl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57062-gpgv",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57062 low vulnerability for gpgv package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CMS (Cryptographic Message Syntax) parsing in gpgsm in GnuPG through 2.5.20 mishandles the CMS format for AES-GCM because aes-ICVlen is supposed to be 12 bytes but 4 bytes is accepted. NOTE: this is related to CVE-2026-34182."
              },
